  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 104.78 Universal waste",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 104.78 “Universal waste” means any of the following hazardous wastes that may be managed in accordance with Env-Hw 1100 in lieu of Env-Hw 300 through Env-Hw 700:\n\n(a) Batteries;\n\n(b) Pesticides;\n\n(c) Mercury-containing devices;\n\n(d) Lamps;\n\n(e) Cathode ray tubes;\n\n(f) Antifreeze; and\n\n(g) Aerosol cans.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Hw 100) #12343, eff 8-14-17; ss by #13405, eff 7-23-22 (formerly Env-Hw 104.72) (See Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-Hw 100) (formerly Env-Hw 104.76)",
